\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {14.2}{\ignorespaces Flat beam of \citet  {he2023mfsnlrom}. (a) Centre displacement over $\pm 2000$\nobreakspace  {}Pa: nonlinear FE, multi-fidelity surrogate and ICE ($R^2=1.0000\xspace  $ and $1.0000\xspace  $ against FE). (b) Free decay of the first modal coordinate ($R^2=0.9971\xspace  $ for case a and $0.9899\xspace  $ for case b). (c) Backbone by harmonic balance against FE free vibration; largest frequency error $0.96\,\%\xspace  $ over a hardening of $21.9\,\%\xspace  $ above the linear frequency. One surrogate evaluation takes $5.0\times 10^{-5}$\xspace  {}\nobreakspace  {}s against 0.84\xspace  {}\nobreakspace  {}s for FE, a ratio of $1.7\times 10^{4}$\xspace  . Redrawn by \texttt  {scripts/ch14\_assets.py} from the saved outputs of the study; the study itself was not re-run for this book.\relax }}{144}{figure.caption.249}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:vf-mfs}{{14.2}{144}{Flat beam of \citet {he2023mfsnlrom}. (a) Centre displacement over $\pm 2000$~Pa: nonlinear FE, multi-fidelity surrogate and ICE ($R^2=\cvfMfsRtwoMfs $ and $\cvfMfsRtwoIce $ against FE). (b) Free decay of the first modal coordinate ($R^2=\cvfMfsDecayA $ for case a and $\cvfMfsDecayB $ for case b). (c) Backbone by harmonic balance against FE free vibration; largest frequency error $\cvfMfsBackErr $ over a hardening of $\cvfMfsHardening $ above the linear frequency. One surrogate evaluation takes \cvfMfsTmfs {}~s against \cvfMfsTfe {}~s for FE, a ratio of \cvfMfsSpeed . Redrawn by \texttt {scripts/ch14\_assets.py} from the saved outputs of the study; the study itself was not re-run for this book.\relax }{figure.caption.249}{}}
